        "assessment": [
          "EVALUATION FOR THE SKILLS AND THE CONTENT: PERFORMANCE ASSIGNMENT: Students will explore the jobs, work routines, and homes of their extended family members and create a fun and creative project to share with the class. They will first talk to their family members such as parents, grandparents, aunts, or uncles, cousins, and ask about their jobs and where they work. They will learn about what they do every day and the type of house they live in, such as an apartment, a house, or a farmhouse. Then, they will draw a family tree or map by showing each family member’s job and workplace. They will add colourful pictures of the different types of houses they live in and include one interesting fact about their routines or homes. Finally, they will write a short story about a day in their family’s life how everyone’s work and daily routines connect by highlighting. They will present their project to the class. The assignment will be evaluated by using a rubric scheme, a rating scale, and/or a marking scheme."
        ]
